Implements a TweakDB writer making it possible to create Tweak databases from scratch.

The writer currently supports the following types:

- `Bool` / `Int8` / `Uint8`
- `Int16` / `Uint16`
- `Int32` / `Uint32`
- `Int64` / `Uint64`
- `Float`
- `CName`
- `String`
- `Color`
- `EulerAngles`
- `Quaternion`
- `Vector2`
- `Vector3`
- `Array<T>`

Not supported:

- `TweakDBID`
- `gamedataLocKeyWrapper`
- `raRef<CResource>`

## Examples

```csharp
var db = new TweakDB();

db.Add("WolvenKit.SomeBoolTrue", new CBool { Value = true });
db.Add("WolvenKit.SomeBoolFalse", new CBool { Value = false });
db.Add("WolvenKit.AnotherBoolTrue", new CBool { Value = true });
db.Add("WolvenKit.SomeInt32", new CInt32 { Value = 20210818 });
db.Add("WolvenKit.SomeFloat", new CFloat { Value = 123.321f });
db.Add("WolvenKit.SomeCName", new CName { Text = "Hello rfuzzo!" });
db.Add("WolvenKit.SomeString", new CString { Text = "H3ll0" });

db.Add("WolvenKit.SomeColor", new CColor
{
    Red = new CUint8 { Value = 100 },
    Green = new CUint8 { Value = 25 },
    Blue = new CUint8 { Value = 175 },
    Alpha = new CUint8 { Value = 125 }
});

db.Add("WolvenKit.SomeVector3", new CVector3
{
    X = new CFloat { Value = 21.11f },
    Y = new CFloat { Value = 20.08f },
    Z = new CFloat { Value = 21.20f }
});

db.Add("WolvenKit.SomeArray<Bool>", new CArray<CBool>
{
    Items = new List<CBool>
    {
        new CBool { Value = false },
        new CBool { Value = true }
    }
});

db.Save("tweakdb_delta.bin");
```

